<% content_for :title, "Impulsivity, Bipolar & Addiction | Bipolar Sober" %>

<main class="addiction-impulsivity-page">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="addiction-impulsivity-hero">
    <div class="addiction-impulsivity-hero-content">

      <p class="addiction-impulsivity-eyebrow">
        BIPOLAR SOBER / ADDICTION / IMPULSIVITY
      </p>

      <h1>
        <span>FUCK IT.</span>
        <span>I WANT IT</span>
        <span>RIGHT NOW.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="addiction-impulsivity-intro">
        THE URGE IS FAST.<br>
        THE CONSEQUENCES AREN'T.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 01 -->
  <section class="addiction-impulsivity-section ai-pink">

    <div class="addiction-impulsivity-heading">
      <p class="ai-number">01 / IMPULSIVITY</p>

      <h2>
        URGE.<br>
        ACTION.<br>
        OH FUCK.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ai-copy">

      <p class="ai-lead">
        Impulsivity can collapse the distance between wanting
        something and doing it.
      </p>

      <p>
        You see it. You want it. You feel it. You do it.
      </p>

      <p>
        The brain barely gets a chance to ask what happens tomorrow
        because right now is screaming louder.
      </p>

      <div class="ai-cycle">
        <span>URGE</span>
        <b>→</b>
        <span>ACTION</span>
        <b>→</b>
        <span>RELIEF / RUSH</span>
        <b>→</b>
        <span>CONSEQUENCE</span>
      </div>

      <blockquote>
        THE GOAL ISN'T TO NEVER HAVE AN URGE.<br>
        IT'S TO PUT SOME FUCKING SPACE BEFORE THE ACTION.
      </blockquote>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 02 -->
  <section class="addiction-impulsivity-section ai-yellow">

    <div class="addiction-impulsivity-heading">
      <p class="ai-number">02 / BIPOLAR</p>

      <h2>
        TURN UP<br>
        THE<br>
        VOLUME.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ai-copy">

      <p class="ai-lead">
        Bipolar symptoms can make an already impulsive brain
        even harder to slow down.
      </p>

      <p>
        Mania or hypomania can bring increased energy, confidence,
        reward-seeking, reduced inhibition, racing thoughts,
        and a feeling that consequences either don't matter
        or simply aren't going to happen.
      </p>

      <p>
        Depression can create a different kind of impulsivity:
        fuck it, nothing matters anyway.
      </p>

      <p>
        And addiction has its own urgency.
      </p>

      <p>
        Put them together and the distance between
        <strong>"I want this"</strong> and
        <strong>"I did this"</strong> can get very fucking short.
      </p>

      <blockquote>
        AN EXPLANATION CAN HELP YOU BUILD A PLAN.<br>
        IT DOESN'T ERASE THE CONSEQUENCES.
      </blockquote>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 03 -->
  <section class="addiction-impulsivity-section ai-black">

    <div class="addiction-impulsivity-heading">
      <p class="ai-number">03 / WHAT IT LOOKS LIKE</p>

      <h2>
        SAME<br>
        ENGINE.<br>
        NEW TARGET.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ai-copy">

      <p class="ai-lead">
        Impulsivity doesn't always attach itself to the same thing.
      </p>

      <div class="ai-behaviors">

        <div>
          <span>DRINKING</span>
          <p>
            I want relief, escape, numbness, excitement,
            or just one fucking drink.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>SHOPPING</span>
          <p>
            I want the rush of finding it, buying it,
            owning it, and feeling different for a minute.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>SPENDING</span>
          <p>
            Future-me can deal with the money.
            Present-me wants the thing.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>WEED</span>
          <p>
            I want my brain to change states right now.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>STEALING ALCOHOL</span>
          <p>
            The urge gets so loud that getting the alcohol
            starts feeling more important than the risk,
            consequences, or everything that comes after.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p>
        Different behavior. Same basic pattern:
        immediate reward beats delayed consequence.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 04 -->
  <section class="addiction-impulsivity-section ai-purple">

    <div class="addiction-impulsivity-heading">
      <p class="ai-number">04 / THE RUSH</p>

      <h2>
        IT WORKS.<br>
        FOR A<br>
        MINUTE.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ai-copy">

      <p class="ai-lead">
        There's a reason impulsive shit can be hard to stop:
        sometimes it gives you exactly what you wanted.
      </p>

      <p>
        The purchase feels exciting.
        The drink changes how you feel.
        Weed changes your mental state.
        Getting away with something can create its own rush.
      </p>

      <p>
        That's part of what makes the cycle convincing.
      </p>

      <p>
        The problem isn't necessarily that there was no reward.
      </p>

      <p>
        The problem is that the reward was immediate
        and the bill showed up later.
      </p>

      <div class="ai-now-later">

        <div>
          <span>RIGHT NOW</span>
          <p>
            Relief. Excitement. Escape. Rush. Numbness.
          </p>
        </div>

        <b>VS.</b>

        <div>
          <span>LATER</span>
          <p>
            Money. Shame. Conflict. Risk. Legal consequences.
            Relapse. Cleanup.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 05 -->
  <section class="addiction-impulsivity-section ai-pink">

    <div class="addiction-impulsivity-heading">
      <p class="ai-number">05 / THE FUCK-IT MOMENT</p>

      <h2>
        CATCH<br>
        THE<br>
        SENTENCE.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ai-copy">

      <p class="ai-lead">
        There is often a tiny sentence between the urge
        and the action.
      </p>

      <div class="ai-thoughts">

        <p>"JUST THIS ONCE."</p>
        <p>"I DESERVE IT."</p>
        <p>"I'LL FIX IT TOMORROW."</p>
        <p>"WHO FUCKING CARES?"</p>
        <p>"NOTHING BAD IS GOING TO HAPPEN."</p>
        <p>"I ALREADY FUCKED UP, SO FUCK IT."</p>
        <p>"I NEED THIS."</p>

      </div>

      <p>
        That sentence matters because it can be the moment
        your brain turns an urge into permission.
      </p>

      <blockquote>
        CATCH THE PERMISSION SLIP<br>
        BEFORE YOU SIGN THE FUCKING THING.
      </blockquote>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 06 -->
  <section class="addiction-impulsivity-section ai-yellow">

    <div class="addiction-impulsivity-heading">
      <p class="ai-number">06 / CREATE FRICTION</p>

      <h2>
        MAKE IT<br>
        HARDER TO<br>
        FUCK UP.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ai-copy">

      <p class="ai-lead">
        You don't have to rely on willpower while your brain
        is screaming at you.
      </p>

      <p>
        Build obstacles before you need them.
      </p>

      <div class="ai-friction-grid">

        <div>
          <span>MONEY</span>
          <p>
            Remove saved cards. Lower spending access.
            Wait before purchases.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>SHOPPING</span>
          <p>
            Put it in the cart. Don't check out yet.
            Make yourself come back later.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>ALCOHOL</span>
          <p>
            Avoid the places and situations where getting alcohol
            becomes easy or automatic.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>WEED</span>
          <p>
            Remove access instead of expecting yourself
            to debate the urge every time it appears.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>PEOPLE</span>
          <p>
            Tell somebody before you act,
            not after everything has already gone sideways.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>TIME</span>
          <p>
            Delay the decision. Even ten minutes creates
            more distance than zero.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <blockquote>
        FRICTION BUYS TIME.<br>
        TIME GIVES YOU OPTIONS.
      </blockquote>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 07 -->
  <section class="addiction-impulsivity-section ai-purple">

    <div class="addiction-impulsivity-heading">
      <p class="ai-number">07 / CHECK THE MOOD</p>

      <h2>
        IS THIS<br>
        JUST AN<br>
        URGE?
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ai-copy">

      <p class="ai-lead">
        With bipolar disorder, a sudden explosion in impulsivity
        can also be information.
      </p>

      <p>
        Is spending suddenly escalating?
      </p>

      <p>
        Are you sleeping less?
        Feeling unusually powerful?
        Taking more risks?
        Talking faster?
        Starting a thousand things?
      </p>

      <p>
        Or are you sinking into depression and reaching for anything
        that makes you feel different?
      </p>

      <p>
        The behavior may be more than an isolated bad decision.
        It may be part of a larger change in your mood.
      </p>

      <blockquote>
        DON'T JUST ASK:<br>
        "WHY DO I WANT THIS?"<br><br>
        ASK:<br>
        "WHAT THE FUCK IS MY MOOD DOING?"
      </blockquote>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 08 -->
  <section class="addiction-impulsivity-section ai-black">

    <div class="addiction-impulsivity-heading">
      <p class="ai-number">08 / THE PAUSE</p>

      <h2>
        DON'T<br>
        DECIDE<br>
        YET.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ai-copy">

      <p class="ai-lead">
        The pause doesn't have to magically make the urge disappear.
      </p>

      <p>
        It just has to stop the urge from becoming an action
        for a little longer.
      </p>

      <div class="ai-pause">

        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <p><strong>NAME IT.</strong><br>I am having an urge.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <p><strong>DELAY IT.</strong><br>I don't have to decide yet.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <p><strong>CHANGE LOCATION.</strong><br>Get away from the opportunity.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <p><strong>CHECK THE MOOD.</strong><br>What else has changed?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>05</span>
          <p><strong>TELL SOMEBODY.</strong><br>Get the urge out of your head and into words.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>06</span>
          <p><strong>PLAY THE TAPE FORWARD.</strong><br>What happens after the rush?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>07</span>
          <p><strong>CHOOSE AGAIN.</strong><br>What do I actually want for myself?</p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- ENDING -->
  <section class="addiction-impulsivity-ending">

    <div>

      <p class="ai-ending-small">
        THE URGE WANTS AN ANSWER RIGHT NOW.
      </p>

      <h2>
        YOU DON'T<br>
        HAVE TO<br>
        <span>GIVE IT ONE.</span>
      </h2>

    </div>

    <div class="ai-ending-copy">

      <p>
        You can want the drink and not drink it.
      </p>

      <p>
        You can want to buy the thing and leave it there.
      </p>

      <p>
        You can want to get high and let the urge pass.
      </p>

      <p>
        You can have the impulse without turning it
        into another consequence.
      </p>

      <p>
        Every little bit of space between impulse and action
        gives you another chance to choose what happens next.
      </p>

      <%= link_to "← BACK TO ADDICTION",
          addiction_path,
          class: "ai-back-button" %>

    </div>

  </section>

</main>